                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "45ababac-007e-4a8e-81c0-57e09613c9b0",
                        "source_entry_id": "9bfbec87-e0de-3f9b-a8bf-c33ad9ce8360",
                        "source_sense_id": "b9aa4310-1e01-3baa-8040-c44938b6faa2",
                        "target_lang_word": "tasty",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tasty",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1576d5fc-3a09-3fc2-a2c0-b6d298c5a282",
                                        "entry_id": "5a2f319e-dc01-362c-bab1-846fdbe27df7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a pleasant or satisfying flavor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f0559ab-20de-4ff1-a096-74d517ed7780",
                                                "sense_id": "1576d5fc-3a09-3fc2-a2c0-b6d298c5a282",
                                                "text": "You could make this tasty meal for breakfast."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0bb2ba8-0729-460d-ba72-7c84ba13e71a",
                                                "sense_id": "1576d5fc-3a09-3fc2-a2c0-b6d298c5a282",
                                                "text": "Now, with all these provisos in mind, what’s the best way to put spinach to work? All due respect to Popeye, a can may not be the tastiest way to introduce it to your table. […] Lightly sautéing fresh spinach in a drizzle of olive or avocado oil meets this baseline, and it’s tasty and nutritious as well."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6f4d08a-a451-4c68-b9e3-431cbf2b17b0",
                                                "sense_id": "1576d5fc-3a09-3fc2-a2c0-b6d298c5a282",
                                                "text": "As Trevor Corson, author of “The Story of Sushi” explains, in Japan, sushi is typically eaten at a bar, where it’s customary for the customer to chat with the chef, who can recommend what’s in season. The short window during which the fish is fresh also makes it more likely to be tastier in Japan."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99ee6314-5087-3f5c-a5a4-1446d7b7ed8b",
                                        "entry_id": "5a2f319e-dc01-362c-bab1-846fdbe27df7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having or showing good taste; tasteful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "537673bc-349e-481f-8565-ee33fd4ffe9a",
                                                "sense_id": "99ee6314-5087-3f5c-a5a4-1446d7b7ed8b",
                                                "text": "These items will make an attractive and tasty display."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d96e243-89ab-49df-8911-dbf5b3320335",
                                                "sense_id": "99ee6314-5087-3f5c-a5a4-1446d7b7ed8b",
                                                "text": "we wait until the palace is half-way up, and then we pay some tasty architect to run us up an ornamental mud hovel, right against it"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e0f979ff-118e-3731-84a3-45e7767b491e",
                                        "entry_id": "5a2f319e-dc01-362c-bab1-846fdbe27df7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Appealing; when applied to persons, sexually appealing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58c75836-0ef3-4545-a0f3-05b34ea7f4a4",
                                                "sense_id": "e0f979ff-118e-3731-84a3-45e7767b491e",
                                                "text": "Country fans probably remember Stu best for a tasty tune he wrote and recorded but didn't want released."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "10e76f97-e6c4-38ff-bb3f-43c4351f6e37",
                                        "entry_id": "5a2f319e-dc01-362c-bab1-846fdbe27df7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Skillful; highly competent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "58c5d0d4-4cac-3e1f-8d6a-c98e4766cc06",
                                        "entry_id": "5a2f319e-dc01-362c-bab1-846fdbe27df7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Potentially violent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6bc7bf5-c946-4f59-bada-ed507b6e9386",
                                                "sense_id": "58c5d0d4-4cac-3e1f-8d6a-c98e4766cc06",
                                                "text": "I watched it all unfold live on Sky News. Ed Miliband was there, but so were the usual bunch of troublemakers and I, for one, was expecting it to kick off.¶ Sure enough, it all got a bit tasty in the afternoon at about the time I should have been polishing off my tinned tuna. Only there was no one about to dish out my grub.¶ They were all glued to the telly watching a gang of blokes wearing balaclavas smash the windows of a Porsche showroom in Park Lane."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1871557b-aa95-4b09-897a-a256eabf66cc",
                                                "sense_id": "58c5d0d4-4cac-3e1f-8d6a-c98e4766cc06",
                                                "text": "No, I wouldn't take a bullet for him, or any of them,I wasn't paid enough to go that far, but I would break up a scrap if it all got a bit tasty and, yeah, it was a great at the bar that night getting the drinks in."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03ccb3a5-c10f-453b-a64e-e185cc01fba1",
                                                "sense_id": "58c5d0d4-4cac-3e1f-8d6a-c98e4766cc06",
                                                "text": "These empires of rusting metal have long been portrayed in film, fiction and TV as a haunt of the wide boy, the tasty geezer, and many other variants of ne'er-do-well"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tasty",
